{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require every baby changing room to have a toilet for the parent",
        "additional_details": "I believe having a toilet in a baby changing room would also help families. As a mother who has had a baby and a small toddler, it\u2019s impossible to take your baby in the pram, or carry them into a toilet cubicle to help your toilet trained toddler. I want to be able to use the toilet, knowing that baby is safely in their pram, within my sight. \u201cFamily changing rooms\u201d should include a nappy changing station, a toilet and a sink, meaning that every member of the family can go to the toilet safely.",
        "background": "I want it to be mandatory that every baby changing room should have a toilet. If you are out on your own, with your baby, and you need the toilet, there is usually nowhere to go. You can\u2019t leave your baby and use the women\u2019s/men\u2019s toilet, and 80% of baby changing rooms I\u2019ve used don\u2019t have a toilet.",
